IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc14-part122-warrants.l4 -- PART XII.2 "Proceeds of Crime", ss 462.32 to 462.36 (special search warrants; restraint orders; management orders; review; expiration) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Imports the keel's core (`ccc-core`) and `daydate` (dates are `Date day month year`).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
-- HOW A RESULT READS: JUST TRUE = the text brings the case within the provision; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = not covered (see NOTES.md).
-- Provisions that address only an official (a judge, the Attorney General, a peace officer, the clerk of the court) are encoded for what they decide; the seat layer asks them from the position of the person whose property or case it is.
-- A "judge" here is the judge of section 462.3(1): its answer is a fact the caller states (every function below takes `the judge` as the actor and the facts as BOOLEAN inputs).

§ `PART XII.2 -- Proceeds of Crime: search, seizure and detention (ss 462.32 to 462.36)`

§§ `s 462.32 -- Special search warrant`

-- src:8031 | 462.32 (1) Subject to subsection (3), if a judge, on application of the Attorney General, is satisfied by information on oath in Form 1 that there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is in any building, receptacle or place any property that is proceeds of crime, the judge may issue a warrant authorizing a person named in the warrant or a peace officer to
-- src:8032 | (a) search the building, receptacle or place for that property; and
-- src:8033 | (b) seize that property and any other property that that person or peace officer believes, on reasonable grounds, is proceeds of crime.
@ref s 462.32(1) (src:8031-8033)
GIVEN `the application is made by the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is in any building, receptacle or place any property that is proceeds of crime` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.32(1) the judge may issue a warrant to search for and seize property that is proceeds of crime` MEANS
    IF `the application is made by the Attorney General`
        AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 1`
        AND `there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is in any building, receptacle or place any property that is proceeds of crime`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if a judge, on application of the Attorney General, is satisfied by information on oath in Form 1 that there are reasonable grounds to believe that there is in any building, receptacle or place any property that is proceeds of crime, the judge may issue a warrant"

DECLARE `s 462.32(1) authorized act` IS ONE OF
    `s 462.32(1)(a) search the building, receptacle or place for that property`
    `s 462.32(1)(b) seize that property and any other property that that person or peace officer believes, on reasonable grounds, is proceeds of crime`
    `s 462.32(1) an act that is none of those named`

@ref s 462.32(1) (src:8031-8033)
GIVEN act IS A `s 462.32(1) authorized act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.32(1) the warrant may authorize the act` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 462.32(1) an act that is none of those named` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "authorizing a person named in the warrant or a peace officer to"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:8035 | (2) An application for a warrant under subsection (1) may be made ex parte, shall be made in writing and shall include a statement as to whether any previous applications have been made under subsection (1) with respect to the property that is the subject of the application.
@ref s 462.32(2) (src:8035)
GIVEN `the application is made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application includes a statement as to whether any previous applications have been made under subsection (1) with respect to the property that is the subject of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.32(2) the application complies with subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the application is made in writing` AND `the application includes a statement as to whether any previous applications have been made under subsection (1) with respect to the property that is the subject of the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be made in writing and shall include a statement as to whether any previous applications have been made under subsection (1)"

@ref s 462.32(2) (src:8035)
GIVEN `the application is for a warrant under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.32(2) the application may be made ex parte` MEANS
    IF `the application is for a warrant under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application for a warrant under subsection (1) may be made ex parte"

-- src:8037 | (2.01) A warrant issued under subsection (1) may be subject to any reasonable conditions that the judge thinks fit.
@ref s 462.32(2.01) (src:8037)
GIVEN `the judge thinks the condition fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.32(2.01) the warrant may be subject to the condition` MEANS
    IF `the judge thinks the condition fit` AND `the condition is reasonable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any reasonable conditions that the judge thinks fit"

-- src:8039 | (2.1) A warrant issued under subsection (1) may be executed at any place in Canada. Any peace officer who executes the warrant must have authority to act as a peace officer in the place where it is executed.
@ref s 462.32(2.1) (src:8039)
GIVEN `the place is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.32(2.1) the warrant may be executed at the place` MEANS
    IF `the place is in Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be executed at any place in Canada"

@ref s 462.32(2.1) (src:8039)
GIVEN `the peace officer has authority to act as a peace officer in the place where the warrant is executed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.32(2.1) the peace officer is barred from executing the warrant at the place` MEANS
    IF `the peace officer has authority to act as a peace officer in the place where the warrant is executed`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any peace officer who executes the warrant must have authority to act as a peace officer in the place where it is executed"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

