-- src:8044 | (4) Every person who executes a warrant issued by a judge under this section shall
-- src:8045 | (a) during that execution, give the following to any person who is present and ostensibly in control of the building, receptacle or place to be searched or, in the absence of any such person, affix the following in a prominent location within the building or place or on or next to the receptacle:
-- src:8046 | (i) a copy of the warrant, and
-- src:8047 | (ii) a notice in Form 5.1 setting out the address of the court from which a copy of the report on the property seized may be obtained;
-- src:8048 | (a.1) detain or cause to be detained the property seized, taking reasonable care to ensure that the property is preserved so that it may be dealt with in accordance with the law;
-- src:8049 | (b) as soon as practicable after the execution of the warrant but within a period not exceeding seven days thereafter, prepare a report in Form 5.3, identifying the property seized and the location where the property is being detained, and cause the report to be filed with the clerk of the court; and
-- src:8050 | (c) cause a copy of the report to be provided, on request, to the person from whom the property was seized and to any other person who, in the opinion of the judge, appears to have a valid interest in the property.
@ref s 462.32(4)(a) to (c) (src:8044-8050)
GIVEN `a person is present who is ostensibly in control of the building, receptacle or place to be searched` IS A BOOLEAN
      `during that execution, the person executing the warrant gave that person a copy of the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `during that execution, the person executing the warrant gave that person a notice in Form 5.1 setting out the address of the court from which a copy of the report on the property seized may be obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the absence of any such person, the person executing the warrant affixed a copy of the warrant and a notice in Form 5.1 in a prominent location within the building or place or on or next to the receptacle` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.32(4)(a) the person executing the warrant has given or affixed the copy and the notice` MEANS
    IF `a person is present who is ostensibly in control of the building, receptacle or place to be searched`
    THEN (IF `during that execution, the person executing the warrant gave that person a copy of the warrant`
              AND `during that execution, the person executing the warrant gave that person a notice in Form 5.1 setting out the address of the court from which a copy of the report on the property seized may be obtained`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who executes a warrant issued by a judge under this section shall"
    ELSE (IF `in the absence of any such person, the person executing the warrant affixed a copy of the warrant and a notice in Form 5.1 in a prominent location within the building or place or on or next to the receptacle`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of any such person, affix the following in a prominent location"

@ref s 462.32(4)(a.1) (src:8048)
GIVEN `the person executing the warrant detained or caused to be detained the property seized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `taking reasonable care to ensure that the property is preserved so that it may be dealt with in accordance with the law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.32(4)(a.1) the person executing the warrant has detained the property seized` MEANS
    IF `the person executing the warrant detained or caused to be detained the property seized` AND `taking reasonable care to ensure that the property is preserved so that it may be dealt with in accordance with the law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "detain or cause to be detained the property seized, taking reasonable care to ensure that the property is preserved"

@ref s 462.32(4)(b) (src:8049)
GIVEN `the date the warrant was executed` IS A DATE
      `the date the report in Form 5.3 was filed with the clerk of the court` IS A DATE
      `the report identifies the property seized and the location where the property is being detained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report was prepared as soon as practicable after the execution of the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.32(4)(b) the report was prepared and filed in time` MEANS
    IF `the report identifies the property seized and the location where the property is being detained` AND `the report was prepared as soon as practicable after the execution of the warrant`
        AND `the date the report in Form 5.3 was filed with the clerk of the court` AT MOST Date (Day `the date the warrant was executed` PLUS 7)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within a period not exceeding seven days thereafter"

@ref s 462.32(4)(c) (src:8050)
GIVEN `the person who asks is the person from whom the property was seized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who asks is another person who, in the opinion of the judge, appears to have a valid interest in the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.32(4)(c) the person executing the warrant must cause a copy of the report to be provided on request` MEANS
    IF `the person who asks is the person from whom the property was seized` OR `the person who asks is another person who, in the opinion of the judge, appears to have a valid interest in the property`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the person from whom the property was seized and to any other person who, in the opinion of the judge, appears to have a valid interest in the property"

-- The duty of paragraph (b) as a regulative rule: the peace officer who executed the warrant MUST file the report WITHIN 7 (days, counted from the execution of the warrant).
DECLARE `s 462.32(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 462.32(4)(b) prepare the report in Form 5.3 and cause it to be filed with the clerk of the court`

@ref s 462.32(4)(b) (src:8049)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 462.32(4) act`
`s 462.32(4)(b) the duty to file the report` MEANS
    PARTY `a peace officer`
    MUST `s 462.32(4)(b) prepare the report in Form 5.3 and cause it to be filed with the clerk of the court`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the report in Form 5.3 was not filed with the clerk of the court within seven days of the execution of the warrant"

-- src:8052 | (4.1) Subject to this or any other Act of Parliament, a peace officer who has seized anything under a warrant issued by a judge under this section may, with the written consent of the Attorney General, on being issued a receipt for it, return the thing seized to the person lawfully entitled to its possession, if
-- src:8053 | (a) the peace officer is satisfied that there is no dispute as to who is lawfully entitled to possession of the thing seized;
-- src:8054 | (b) the peace officer is satisfied that the continued detention of the thing seized is not required for the purpose of forfeiture; and
-- src:8055 | (c) the thing seized is returned before a report is filed with the clerk of the court under paragraph (4)(b).
@ref s 462.32(4.1) (src:8052-8055)
GIVEN `the peace officer has the written consent of the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer has been issued a receipt for the thing seized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer is satisfied that there is no dispute as to who is lawfully entitled to possession of the thing seized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer is satisfied that the continued detention of the thing seized is not required for the purpose of forfeiture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing seized is returned before a report is filed with the clerk of the court under paragraph (4)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.32(4.1) the peace officer may return the thing seized to the person lawfully entitled to its possession` MEANS
    IF NOT `the peace officer has been issued a receipt for the thing seized`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on being issued a receipt for it" (a gate of the kind "on payment" on a power: listed in the fork register, F35)
    ELSE IF `the peace officer has the written consent of the Attorney General`
            AND `the peace officer is satisfied that there is no dispute as to who is lawfully entitled to possession of the thing seized`   -- (a)
            AND `the peace officer is satisfied that the continued detention of the thing seized is not required for the purpose of forfeiture`   -- (b)
            AND `the thing seized is returned before a report is filed with the clerk of the court under paragraph (4)(b)`   -- (c)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, with the written consent of the Attorney General, on being issued a receipt for it, return the thing seized to the person lawfully entitled to its possession, if"

-- src:8057 | (5) Before issuing a warrant under this section in relation to any property, a judge may require notice to be given to and may hear any person who, in the opinion of the judge, appears to have a valid interest in the property unless the judge is of the opinion that giving such notice before the issuance of the warrant would result in the disappearance, dissipation or reduction in value of the property or otherwise affect the property so that all or a part thereof could not be seized pursuant to the warrant.
@ref s 462.32(5) (src:8057)
GIVEN `the person appears to the judge to have a valid interest in the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is of the opinion that giving notice before the issuance of the warrant would result in the disappearance, dissipation or reduction in value of the property or otherwise affect the property so that all or a part of it could not be seized pursuant to the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.32(5) the judge may require notice to be given to and may hear the person before issuing the warrant` MEANS
    IF `the judge is of the opinion that giving notice before the issuance of the warrant would result in the disappearance, dissipation or reduction in value of the property or otherwise affect the property so that all or a part of it could not be seized pursuant to the warrant`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the judge is of the opinion that giving such notice before the issuance of the warrant would result in the disappearance, dissipation or reduction in value of the property"
    ELSE IF `the person appears to the judge to have a valid interest in the property`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person who, in the opinion of the judge, appears to have a valid interest in the property"

-- src:8058 | (6) [Repealed, 2024, c. 15, s. 309]
@ref s 462.32(6), shown repealed (src:8058)
`s 462.32(6) as the text shows it` MEANS "(6) [Repealed, 2024, c. 15, s. 309]"

§§ `s 462.321 -- Special warrant -- digital assets`

-- src:8060 | 462.321 (1) If, on an application of the Attorney General, a judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 1, varied to suit the case, that there are reasonable grounds to believe that any digital assets, including virtual currency, are proceeds of crime, the judge may issue a warrant authorizing a person named in the warrant or a peace officer to
-- src:8061 | (a) search for the digital assets by using a computer program, as defined in subsection 342.1(2); and
-- src:8062 | (b) seize — including by taking control of the right to access — the digital assets, as well as any other digital assets found during that search that the person or peace officer believes, on reasonable grounds, are proceeds of crime.
@ref s 462.321(1) (src:8060-8062)
GIVEN `the application is made by the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 1, varied to suit the case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that any digital assets, including virtual currency, are proceeds of crime` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.321(1) the judge may issue a warrant to search for and seize digital assets that are proceeds of crime` MEANS
    IF `the application is made by the Attorney General`
        AND `the judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 1, varied to suit the case`
        AND `there are reasonable grounds to believe that any digital assets, including virtual currency, are proceeds of crime`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If, on an application of the Attorney General, a judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 1, varied to suit the case, that there are reasonable grounds to believe that any digital assets, including virtual currency, are proceeds of crime, the judge may issue a warrant"

DECLARE `s 462.321(1) authorized act` IS ONE OF
    `s 462.321(1)(a) search for the digital assets by using a computer program, as defined in subsection 342.1(2)`
    `s 462.321(1)(b) seize, including by taking control of the right to access, the digital assets, as well as any other digital assets found during that search that the person or peace officer believes, on reasonable grounds, are proceeds of crime`
    `s 462.321(1) an act that is none of those named`

@ref s 462.321(1) (src:8060-8062)
GIVEN act IS A `s 462.321(1) authorized act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.321(1) the warrant may authorize the act` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 462.321(1) an act that is none of those named` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "authorizing a person named in the warrant or a peace officer to"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

