-- src:8070 | (4) Every person who executes a warrant issued by a judge under this section shall
-- src:8071 | (a) detain or cause to be detained any seized property, taking reasonable care to ensure that it is preserved so that it may be dealt with in accordance with the law;
-- src:8072 | (b) as soon as practicable after the execution of the warrant, cause the following to be sent to the usual place of residence of any person from whom the property is seized if that usual place of residence is in Canada and is known to the person executing the warrant:
-- src:8073 | (i) a copy of the warrant, and
-- src:8074 | (ii) a notice in Form 5.1, varied to suit the case, setting out the address of the court from which a copy of a report on the seized property may be obtained;
-- src:8075 | (c) as soon as practicable after the execution of the warrant but within a period of not more than seven days, prepare a report in Form 5.3, varied to suit the case, identifying the seized property and the manner in which it is being detained, and cause the report to be filed with the clerk of the court; and
-- src:8076 | (d) cause a copy of the report to be provided, on request, to the person from whom the property was seized and to any other person who, in the opinion of the judge, appears to have a valid interest in the seized property.
@ref s 462.321(4)(a) to (d) (src:8070-8076)
GIVEN `the person executing the warrant detained or caused to be detained the seized property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `taking reasonable care to ensure that it is preserved so that it may be dealt with in accordance with the law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.321(4)(a) the person executing the warrant has detained the seized property` MEANS
    IF `the person executing the warrant detained or caused to be detained the seized property` AND `taking reasonable care to ensure that it is preserved so that it may be dealt with in accordance with the law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "detain or cause to be detained any seized property, taking reasonable care to ensure that it is preserved"

@ref s 462.321(4)(b) (src:8072-8074)
GIVEN `the usual place of residence of the person from whom the property is seized is in Canada and is known to the person executing the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `as soon as practicable after the execution of the warrant, a copy of the warrant was sent to that usual place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `as soon as practicable after the execution of the warrant, a notice in Form 5.1, varied to suit the case, setting out the address of the court from which a copy of a report on the seized property may be obtained was sent to that usual place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.321(4)(b) the person executing the warrant has sent the copy of the warrant and the notice` MEANS
    IF NOT `the usual place of residence of the person from whom the property is seized is in Canada and is known to the person executing the warrant`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if that usual place of residence is in Canada and is known to the person executing the warrant"
    ELSE IF `as soon as practicable after the execution of the warrant, a copy of the warrant was sent to that usual place of residence`
            AND `as soon as practicable after the execution of the warrant, a notice in Form 5.1, varied to suit the case, setting out the address of the court from which a copy of a report on the seized property may be obtained was sent to that usual place of residence`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "cause the following to be sent to the usual place of residence of any person from whom the property is seized"

@ref s 462.321(4)(c) (src:8075)
GIVEN `the date the warrant was executed` IS A DATE
      `the date the report in Form 5.3 was filed with the clerk of the court` IS A DATE
      `the report identifies the seized property and the manner in which it is being detained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report was prepared as soon as practicable after the execution of the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.321(4)(c) the report was prepared and filed in time` MEANS
    IF `the report identifies the seized property and the manner in which it is being detained` AND `the report was prepared as soon as practicable after the execution of the warrant`
        AND `the date the report in Form 5.3 was filed with the clerk of the court` AT MOST Date (Day `the date the warrant was executed` PLUS 7)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but within a period of not more than seven days"

@ref s 462.321(4)(d) (src:8076)
GIVEN `the person who asks is the person from whom the property was seized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who asks is another person who, in the opinion of the judge, appears to have a valid interest in the seized property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.321(4)(d) the person executing the warrant must cause a copy of the report to be provided on request` MEANS
    IF `the person who asks is the person from whom the property was seized` OR `the person who asks is another person who, in the opinion of the judge, appears to have a valid interest in the seized property`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the person from whom the property was seized and to any other person who, in the opinion of the judge, appears to have a valid interest in the seized property"

DECLARE `s 462.321(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 462.321(4)(c) prepare the report in Form 5.3 and cause it to be filed with the clerk of the court`

@ref s 462.321(4)(c) (src:8075)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 462.321(4) act`
`s 462.321(4)(c) the duty to file the report` MEANS
    PARTY `a peace officer`
    MUST `s 462.321(4)(c) prepare the report in Form 5.3 and cause it to be filed with the clerk of the court`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the report in Form 5.3 was not filed with the clerk of the court within seven days of the execution of the warrant"

-- src:8078 | (5) Subject to this or any other Act of Parliament, a peace officer or a person acting on their behalf may, with the written consent of the Attorney General, on being issued a receipt for it, cause the seized property to be returned to the person lawfully entitled to its possession, if
-- src:8079 | (a) the peace officer is satisfied that there is no dispute as to who is lawfully entitled to possession of the seized property;
-- src:8080 | (b) the peace officer is satisfied that the continued detention of the seized property is not required for the purpose of forfeiture; and
-- src:8081 | (c) the seized property is returned before a report is filed with the clerk of the court under paragraph (4)(c).
@ref s 462.321(5) (src:8078-8081)
GIVEN `the peace officer or a person acting on their behalf has the written consent of the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a receipt for the seized property has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer is satisfied that there is no dispute as to who is lawfully entitled to possession of the seized property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer is satisfied that the continued detention of the seized property is not required for the purpose of forfeiture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seized property is returned before a report is filed with the clerk of the court under paragraph (4)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.321(5) the seized property may be returned to the person lawfully entitled to its possession` MEANS
    IF NOT `a receipt for the seized property has been issued`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on being issued a receipt for it" (a gate of the kind "on payment" on a power: listed in the fork register, F35)
    ELSE IF `the peace officer or a person acting on their behalf has the written consent of the Attorney General`
            AND `the peace officer is satisfied that there is no dispute as to who is lawfully entitled to possession of the seized property`   -- (a)
            AND `the peace officer is satisfied that the continued detention of the seized property is not required for the purpose of forfeiture`   -- (b)
            AND `the seized property is returned before a report is filed with the clerk of the court under paragraph (4)(c)`   -- (c)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, with the written consent of the Attorney General, on being issued a receipt for it, cause the seized property to be returned to the person lawfully entitled to its possession, if"

-- src:8083 | (6) Before issuing a warrant under this section in relation to any property, a judge may require notice to be given to and may hear any person who, in the opinion of the judge, appears to have a valid interest in the property unless the judge is of the opinion that giving such notice before the issuance of the warrant would result in the disappearance, dissipation or reduction in value of the property or otherwise affect the property so that all or a part of it could not be seized under the warrant.
@ref s 462.321(6) (src:8083)
GIVEN `the person appears to the judge to have a valid interest in the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is of the opinion that giving notice before the issuance of the warrant would result in the disappearance, dissipation or reduction in value of the property or otherwise affect the property so that all or a part of it could not be seized under the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.321(6) the judge may require notice to be given to and may hear the person before issuing the warrant` MEANS
    IF `the judge is of the opinion that giving notice before the issuance of the warrant would result in the disappearance, dissipation or reduction in value of the property or otherwise affect the property so that all or a part of it could not be seized under the warrant`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the judge is of the opinion that giving such notice before the issuance of the warrant would result in the disappearance, dissipation or reduction in value of the property"
    ELSE IF `the person appears to the judge to have a valid interest in the property`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person who, in the opinion of the judge, appears to have a valid interest in the property"

-- src:8084 | (7) [Repealed, 2024, c. 15, s. 310]
@ref s 462.321(7), shown repealed (src:8084)
`s 462.321(7) as the text shows it` MEANS "(7) [Repealed, 2024, c. 15, s. 310]"

§§ `s 462.33 -- Application for restraint order`

-- src:8086 | 462.33 (1) The Attorney General may make an application in accordance with subsection (2) for a restraint order under subsection (3) in respect of any property.
@ref s 462.33(1) (src:8086)
GIVEN `the person making the application is the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.33(1) the Attorney General may apply for a restraint order in respect of any property` MEANS
    IF `the person making the application is the Attorney General`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Attorney General may make an application"

-- src:8088 | (2) An application made under subsection (1) for a restraint order under subsection (3) in respect of any property may be made ex parte and shall be made in writing to a judge and be accompanied by an affidavit sworn on the information and belief of the Attorney General or any other person deposing to the following matters, namely,
-- src:8089 | (a) the offence or matter under investigation;
-- src:8090 | (b) the person who is believed to be in possession of the property;
-- src:8091 | (c) the grounds for the belief that the property is proceeds of crime;
-- src:8092 | (d) a description of the property; and
-- src:8093 | (e) whether any previous applications have been made under this section with respect to the property.
@ref s 462.33(2) (src:8088-8093)
GIVEN `the application is made in writing to a judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is accompanied by an affidavit sworn on the information and belief of the Attorney General or any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to the offence or matter under investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to the person who is believed to be in possession of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to the grounds for the belief that the property is proceeds of crime` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to a description of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit deposes to whether any previous applications have been made under section 462.33 with respect to the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.33(2) the application complies with subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the application is made in writing to a judge`
        AND `the application is accompanied by an affidavit sworn on the information and belief of the Attorney General or any other person`
        AND `the affidavit deposes to the offence or matter under investigation`   -- (a)
        AND `the affidavit deposes to the person who is believed to be in possession of the property`   -- (b)
        AND `the affidavit deposes to the grounds for the belief that the property is proceeds of crime`   -- (c)
        AND `the affidavit deposes to a description of the property`   -- (d)
        AND `the affidavit deposes to whether any previous applications have been made under section 462.33 with respect to the property`   -- (e)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be made in writing to a judge and be accompanied by an affidavit sworn on the information and belief of the Attorney General or any other person deposing to the following matters"

@ref s 462.33(2) (src:8088)
GIVEN `the application is made under subsection (1) for a restraint order under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.33(2) the application may be made ex parte` MEANS
    IF `the application is made under subsection (1) for a restraint order under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application made under subsection (1) for a restraint order under subsection (3) in respect of any property may be made ex parte"

-- src:8095 | (3) A judge who hears an application for a restraint order made under subsection (1) may, if the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that there exists any property that is proceeds of crime, make an order prohibiting any person from disposing of, or otherwise dealing with any interest in, the property specified in the order otherwise than in the manner that may be specified in the order.
@ref s 462.33(3) (src:8095)
GIVEN `the judge hears an application for a restraint order made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that there exists any property that is proceeds of crime` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.33(3) the judge may make an order prohibiting any person from disposing of or dealing with any interest in the property` MEANS
    IF `the judge hears an application for a restraint order made under subsection (1)` AND `the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that there exists any property that is proceeds of crime`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, if the judge is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that there exists any property that is proceeds of crime, make an order"

-- src:8097 | (3.01) A restraint order issued under subsection (1) has effect throughout Canada.
@ref s 462.33(3.01) (src:8097)
GIVEN `the restraint order is issued under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.33(3.01) the restraint order has effect throughout Canada` MEANS
    IF `the restraint order is issued under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A restraint order issued under subsection (1) has effect throughout Canada"

-- src:8099 | (3.1) A restraint order may be issued under this section in respect of property situated outside Canada, with any modifications that the circumstances require.
@ref s 462.33(3.1) (src:8099)
GIVEN `the property is situated outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.33(3.1) a restraint order may be issued in respect of the property` MEANS
    IF `the property is situated outside Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of property situated outside Canada"

-- src:8101 | (4) An order made by a judge under subsection (3) may be subject to such reasonable conditions as the judge thinks fit.
@ref s 462.33(4) (src:8101)
GIVEN `the judge thinks the condition fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.33(4) the order may be subject to the condition` MEANS
    IF `the judge thinks the condition fit` AND `the condition is reasonable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such reasonable conditions as the judge thinks fit"

-- src:8103 | (5) Before making an order under subsection (3) in relation to any property, a judge may require notice to be given to and may hear any person who, in the opinion of the judge, appears to have a valid interest in the property unless the judge is of the opinion that giving such notice before making the order would result in the disappearance, dissipation or reduction in value of the property or otherwise affect the property so that all or a part thereof could not be subject to an order of forfeiture under subsection 462.37(1) or (2.01) or 462.38(2).
@ref s 462.33(5) (src:8103)
GIVEN `the person appears to the judge to have a valid interest in the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is of the opinion that giving notice before making the order would result in the disappearance, dissipation or reduction in value of the property or otherwise affect the property so that all or a part of it could not be subject to an order of forfeiture under subsection 462.37(1) or (2.01) or 462.38(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.33(5) the judge may require notice to be given to and may hear the person before making the order` MEANS
    IF `the judge is of the opinion that giving notice before making the order would result in the disappearance, dissipation or reduction in value of the property or otherwise affect the property so that all or a part of it could not be subject to an order of forfeiture under subsection 462.37(1) or (2.01) or 462.38(2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the judge is of the opinion that giving such notice before making the order would result in the disappearance, dissipation or reduction in value of the property"
    ELSE IF `the person appears to the judge to have a valid interest in the property`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person who, in the opinion of the judge, appears to have a valid interest in the property"

-- src:8105 | (6) An order made under subsection (3) shall be made in writing.
@ref s 462.33(6) (src:8105)
GIVEN `the order is made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.33(6) the order complies with subsection (6)` MEANS
    IF `the order is made in writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An order made under subsection (3) shall be made in writing"

-- src:8106 | (7) [Repealed, 2024, c. 15, s. 311]
@ref s 462.33(7), shown repealed (src:8106)
`s 462.33(7) as the text shows it` MEANS "(7) [Repealed, 2024, c. 15, s. 311]"

-- src:8108 | (8) A copy of an order made by a judge under subsection (3) shall be served on the person to whom the order is addressed in such manner as the judge directs or as may be prescribed by rules of court.
@ref s 462.33(8) (src:8108)
GIVEN `a copy of the order was served on the person to whom the order is addressed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was served in such manner as the judge directs or as may be prescribed by rules of court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.33(8) the order has been served as subsection (8) requires` MEANS
    IF `a copy of the order was served on the person to whom the order is addressed` AND `it was served in such manner as the judge directs or as may be prescribed by rules of court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be served on the person to whom the order is addressed in such manner as the judge directs or as may be prescribed by rules of court"

-- src:8110 | (9) A copy of an order made under subsection (3) shall be registered against any property in accordance with the laws of the province in which the property is situated.
@ref s 462.33(9) (src:8110)
GIVEN `a copy of the order was registered against the property in accordance with the laws of the province in which the property is situated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.33(9) the order has been registered as subsection (9) requires` MEANS
    IF `a copy of the order was registered against the property in accordance with the laws of the province in which the property is situated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be registered against any property in accordance with the laws of the province in which the property is situated"

-- src:8112 | (10) An order made under subsection (3) remains in effect until
-- src:8113 | (a) it is revoked or varied under subsection 462.34(4) or revoked under paragraph 462.43(a);
-- src:8114 | (b) it ceases to be in force under section 462.35; or
-- src:8115 | (c) an order of forfeiture or restoration of the property is made under subsection 462.37(1) or (2.01), 462.38(2) or 462.41(3) or any other provision of this or any other Act of Parliament.
@ref s 462.33(10) (src:8112-8115)
GIVEN `it is revoked or varied under subsection 462.34(4) or revoked under paragraph 462.43(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it ceases to be in force under section 462.35` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order of forfeiture or restoration of the property is made under subsection 462.37(1) or (2.01), 462.38(2) or 462.41(3) or any other provision of this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.33(10) the order remains in effect` MEANS
    IF `it is revoked or varied under subsection 462.34(4) or revoked under paragraph 462.43(a)`   -- (a)
        OR `it ceases to be in force under section 462.35`   -- (b)
        OR `an order of forfeiture or restoration of the property is made under subsection 462.37(1) or (2.01), 462.38(2) or 462.41(3) or any other provision of this or any other Act of Parliament`   -- (c)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An order made under subsection (3) remains in effect until"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:8117 | (11) Any person on whom an order made under subsection (3) is served in accordance with this section and who, while the order is in force, acts in contravention of or fails to comply with the order is guilty of an indictable offence or an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 462.33(11) (src:8117)
GIVEN `the person was served with the order in accordance with section 462.33` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts in contravention of or fails to comply with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.33(11) the person commits the offence of contravening a restraint order` MEANS
    IF `the person was served with the order in accordance with section 462.33` AND `the order is in force` AND `the person acts in contravention of or fails to comply with the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person on whom an order made under subsection (3) is served in accordance with this section and who, while the order is in force, acts in contravention of or fails to comply with the order"

@ref s 462.33(11) (src:8117)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 462.33(11) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- The section states no term and no fine for either limb ("guilty of an indictable offence or an offence punishable on summary conviction").
@ref s 462.33(11) (src:8117)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 462.33(11) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
       , (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)

§§ `s 462.331 -- Management order`

-- src:8119 | 462.331 (1) With respect to property seized under section 462.32 or 462.321 or restrained under section 462.33, other than a controlled substance, within the meaning of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act, or cannabis, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Cannabis Act, on application of the Attorney General or of any other person with the written consent of the Attorney General, if a judge is of the opinion that the circumstances so require, the judge may
-- src:8120 | (a) appoint a person to take control of and to manage or otherwise deal with all or part of the property in accordance with the directions of the judge; and
-- src:8121 | (b) require any person having possession of that property to give possession of the property to the person appointed under paragraph (a).
@ref s 462.331(1) (src:8119-8121)
GIVEN `the property is seized under section 462.32 or 462.321 or restrained under section 462.33` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is a controlled substance, within the meaning of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act, or cannabis, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Cannabis Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the Attorney General, or by any other person with the written consent of the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is of the opinion that the circumstances so require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.331(1) the judge may appoint a person to take control of and manage the property and require any person having possession of it to give possession` MEANS
    IF `the property is a controlled substance, within the meaning of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act, or cannabis, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Cannabis Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than a controlled substance, within the meaning of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act, or cannabis"
    ELSE IF NOT `the application is made by the Attorney General, or by any other person with the written consent of the Attorney General`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application of the Attorney General or of any other person with the written consent of the Attorney General" (a gate of the kind "on application" on a power: listed in the fork register, F35)
         ELSE IF `the property is seized under section 462.32 or 462.321 or restrained under section 462.33`
                 AND `the judge is of the opinion that the circumstances so require`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if a judge is of the opinion that the circumstances so require, the judge may"

-- src:8123 | (2) When the Attorney General of Canada so requests, a judge appointing a person under subsection (1) shall appoint the Minister of Public Works and Government Services.
@ref s 462.331(2) (src:8123)
GIVEN `the Attorney General of Canada so requests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is appointing a person under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.331(2) the judge must appoint the Minister of Public Works and Government Services` MEANS
    IF `the Attorney General of Canada so requests` AND `the judge is appointing a person under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When the Attorney General of Canada so requests, a judge appointing a person under subsection (1) shall appoint the Minister of Public Works and Government Services"

DECLARE `s 462.331(3) power` IS ONE OF
    `s 462.331(3)(a) make an interlocutory sale of perishable or rapidly depreciating property`
    `s 462.331(3)(b) destroy, in accordance with subsections (4) to (7), property that has little or no value`
    `s 462.331(3)(c) have property, other than real property or a conveyance, forfeited to Her Majesty in accordance with subsection (7.1)`
    `s 462.331(3) a power that is none of those named`

-- src:8125 | (3) The power to manage or otherwise deal with property under subsection (1) includes
-- src:8126 | (a) the power to make an interlocutory sale of perishable or rapidly depreciating property;
-- src:8127 | (b) the power to destroy, in accordance with subsections (4) to (7), property that has little or no value; and
-- src:8128 | (c) the power to have property, other than real property or a conveyance, forfeited to Her Majesty in accordance with subsection (7.1).
@ref s 462.331(3) (src:8125-8128)
GIVEN power IS A `s 462.331(3) power`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.331(3) the power to manage or otherwise deal with property includes the power` MEANS
    CONSIDER power
    WHEN `s 462.331(3) a power that is none of those named` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:8130 | (4) Before a person who is appointed to manage property destroys property that has little or no value, they shall apply to a court for a destruction order.
@ref s 462.331(4) (src:8130)
GIVEN `the property has little or no value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person appointed to manage the property has applied to a court for a destruction order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.331(4) the person appointed is barred from destroying the property` MEANS
    IF NOT `the property has little or no value`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "destroys property that has little or no value"
    ELSE IF `the person appointed to manage the property has applied to a court for a destruction order`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before a person who is appointed to manage property destroys property that has little or no value, they shall apply to a court for a destruction order" (the application has been made)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:8132 | (5) Before making a destruction order, a court shall require notice in accordance with subsection (6) to be given to and may hear any person who, in the court’s opinion, appears to have a valid interest in the property.
@ref s 462.331(5) (src:8132)
GIVEN `the court is about to make a destruction order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person appears to the court to have a valid interest in the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.331(5) the court must require notice to be given to the person` MEANS
    IF `the court is about to make a destruction order` AND `the person appears to the court to have a valid interest in the property`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Before making a destruction order, a court shall require notice in accordance with subsection (6) to be given to and may hear any person who, in the court’s opinion, appears to have a valid interest in the property"

-- src:8134 | (6) A notice shall
-- src:8135 | (a) be given in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court; and
-- src:8136 | (b) specify the effective period of the notice that the court considers reasonable or that may be set out in the rules of the court.
@ref s 462.331(6) (src:8134-8136)
GIVEN `the notice is given in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies the effective period of the notice that the court considers reasonable or that may be set out in the rules of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.331(6) the notice complies with subsection (6)` MEANS
    IF `the notice is given in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court`   -- (a)
        AND `the notice specifies the effective period of the notice that the court considers reasonable or that may be set out in the rules of the court`   -- (b)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice shall"

-- src:8138 | (7) A court shall order that the property be destroyed if it is satisfied that the property has little or no financial or other value.
@ref s 462.331(7) (src:8138)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the property has little or no financial or other value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.331(7) the court must order that the property be destroyed` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that the property has little or no financial or other value`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is satisfied that the property has little or no financial or other value"

-- src:8140 | (7.1) On application by a person who is appointed to manage the property, a court shall order that the property, other than real property or a conveyance, be forfeited to Her Majesty to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with in accordance with the law if
-- src:8141 | (a) a notice is given or published in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court;
-- src:8142 | (b) the notice specifies a period of 60 days during which a person may make an application to the court asserting their interest in the property; and
-- src:8143 | (c) during that period, no one makes such an application.
@ref s 462.331(7.1) (src:8140-8143)
GIVEN `the application is made by a person who is appointed to manage the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is real property or a conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notice is given or published in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days in the period the notice specifies during which a person may make an application asserting their interest in the property` IS A NUMBER
      `during that period, someone makes such an application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.331(7.1) the court must order that the property be forfeited to Her Majesty` MEANS
    IF `the property is real property or a conveyance`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the property, other than real property or a conveyance"
    ELSE IF `the application is made by a person who is appointed to manage the property`
            AND `a notice is given or published in the manner that the court directs or that may be specified in the rules of the court`   -- (a)
            AND `the number of days in the period the notice specifies during which a person may make an application asserting their interest in the property` EQUALS 60   -- (b)
            AND NOT `during that period, someone makes such an application`   -- (c)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "be forfeited to Her Majesty to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with in accordance with the law if"

-- src:8145 | (8) A management order ceases to have effect when the property that is the subject of the management order is returned in accordance with the law, destroyed or forfeited to Her Majesty.
@ref s 462.331(8) (src:8145)
GIVEN `the property that is the subject of the management order is returned in accordance with the law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is forfeited to Her Majesty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.331(8) the management order has ceased to have effect` MEANS
    IF `the property that is the subject of the management order is returned in accordance with the law` OR `the property is destroyed` OR `the property is forfeited to Her Majesty`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A management order ceases to have effect when the property that is the subject of the management order is returned in accordance with the law, destroyed or forfeited to Her Majesty"

-- src:8147 | (8.1) For greater certainty, if property that is the subject of a management order is sold, the management order applies to the net proceeds of the sale.
@ref s 462.331(8.1) (src:8147)
GIVEN `the property that is the subject of a management order is sold` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.331(8.1) the management order applies to the net proceeds of the sale` MEANS
    IF `the property that is the subject of a management order is sold`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if property that is the subject of a management order is sold"

DECLARE `s 462.331(9) application` IS ONE OF
    `s 462.331(9) an application to cancel or vary a condition to which a management order is subject`
    `s 462.331(9) an application to vary an appointment made under subsection (2)`
    `s 462.331(9) an application that is none of those`

-- src:8149 | (9) The Attorney General may at any time apply to the judge to cancel or vary any condition to which a management order is subject but may not apply to vary an appointment made under subsection (2).
@ref s 462.331(9) (src:8149)
GIVEN application IS A `s 462.331(9) application`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.331(9) the Attorney General may apply to the judge` MEANS
    CONSIDER application
    WHEN `s 462.331(9) an application to cancel or vary a condition to which a management order is subject` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 462.331(9) an application to vary an appointment made under subsection (2)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not apply to vary an appointment made under subsection (2)"
    WHEN `s 462.331(9) an application that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of conditions and of an appointment under subsection (2)

§§ `s 462.34 -- Application for review of special warrants and restraint orders`

-- src:8151 | 462.34 (1) Any person who has an interest in property that was seized under a warrant issued under section 462.32 or 462.321 or in respect of which a restraint order was made under subsection 462.33(3) may, at any time, apply to a judge for
-- src:8152 | (a) an order under subsection (4);
-- src:8153 | (b) permission to examine any seized property that does not consist of digital assets; or
-- src:8154 | (c) an order requiring an accounting of any seized digital assets.
@ref s 462.34(1) (src:8151-8154)
GIVEN `the person has an interest in property that was seized under a warrant issued under section 462.32 or 462.321 or in respect of which a restraint order was made under subsection 462.33(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is for an order under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is for permission to examine seized property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is for an order requiring an accounting of seized digital assets` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seized property consists of digital assets` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.34(1) the person may, at any time, apply to a judge` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person has an interest in property that was seized under a warrant issued under section 462.32 or 462.321 or in respect of which a restraint order was made under subsection 462.33(3)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who has an interest in property that was seized under a warrant issued under section 462.32 or 462.321 or in respect of which a restraint order was made under subsection 462.33(3)"
    ELSE IF `the application is for an order under subsection (4)`   -- (a)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `the application is for permission to examine seized property` AND NOT `the seized property consists of digital assets`   -- (b)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE IF `the application is for an order requiring an accounting of seized digital assets` AND `the seized property consists of digital assets`   -- (c)
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "permission to examine any seized property that does not consist of digital assets"

-- The seam the keel's PLAN.md names for ss 83.13 and 83.14: a thin answer, whether a review of the special warrant or restraint order has been applied for (a fact; section 462.34(1) is the provision that gives the right to apply).
-- src:8151 | 462.34 (1) Any person who has an interest in property that was seized under a warrant issued under section 462.32 or 462.321 or in respect of which a restraint order was made under subsection 462.33(3) may, at any time, apply to a judge for
@ref s 462.34(1) (src:8151)
GIVEN `an application has been made to a judge under subsection 462.34(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.34 the review of the special warrant or restraint order has been applied for` MEANS
    IF `an application has been made to a judge under subsection 462.34(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text makes no review available to be inferred from the absence of an application

-- src:8156 | (2) Where an application is made under paragraph (1)(a),
-- src:8157 | (a) the application shall not, without the consent of the Attorney General, be heard by a judge unless the applicant has given to the Attorney General at least two clear days notice in writing of the application; and
-- src:8158 | (b) the judge may require notice of the application to be given to and may hear any person who, in the opinion of the judge, appears to have a valid interest in the property.
@ref s 462.34(2) (src:8156-8158)
GIVEN `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General has consented to the application being heard` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant has given to the Attorney General notice in writing of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of clear days of that notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.34(2)(a) the application is barred from being heard by a judge` MEANS
    IF NOT `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an application is made under paragraph (1)(a)"
    ELSE IF `the Attorney General has consented to the application being heard`
            OR (`the applicant has given to the Attorney General notice in writing of the application` AND `the number of clear days of that notice` AT LEAST 2)
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not, without the consent of the Attorney General, be heard by a judge unless the applicant has given to the Attorney General at least two clear days notice in writing of the application"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 462.34(2)(b) (src:8158)
GIVEN `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person appears to the judge to have a valid interest in the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.34(2)(b) the judge may require notice of the application to be given to and may hear the person` MEANS
    IF NOT `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an application is made under paragraph (1)(a)" (a "where" gate on a power: listed in the fork register, F35)
    ELSE IF `the person appears to the judge to have a valid interest in the property`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person who, in the opinion of the judge, appears to have a valid interest in the property"

-- src:8160 | (3) A judge may, on an application made to the judge under paragraph (1)(b), order that the applicant be permitted to examine property subject to such terms as appear to the judge to be necessary or desirable to ensure that the property is safeguarded and preserved for any purpose for which it may subsequently be required.
@ref s 462.34(3) (src:8160)
GIVEN `the application is made under paragraph (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.34(3) the judge may order that the applicant be permitted to examine the property subject to terms` MEANS
    IF `the application is made under paragraph (1)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on an application made to the judge under paragraph (1)(b)" (a gate of the kind "on such an application" on a power: listed in the fork register, F35)

-- src:8186 | (6) An order under paragraph (4)(b) in respect of property may be made by a judge if the judge is satisfied that the property will no longer be required for the purpose of any investigation or as evidence in any proceeding and
-- src:8187 | (a) that a warrant should not have been issued under section 462.32 or 462.321 or a restraint order under subsection 462.33(3) should not have been made in respect of that property, in the case where the application is made by
-- src:8188 | (i) a person charged with a designated offence, or
-- src:8189 | (ii) any person who acquired title to or a right of possession of that property from a person referred to in subparagraph (i) under circumstances that give rise to a reasonable inference that the title or right was transferred from that person for the purpose of avoiding the forfeiture of the property; or
-- src:8190 | (b) in any other case, that the applicant is the lawful owner of or lawfully entitled to possession of the property and appears innocent of any complicity in a designated offence or of any collusion in relation to such an offence, and that no other person appears to be the lawful owner of or lawfully entitled to possession of the property.
@ref s 462.34(6) (src:8186-8190)
GIVEN `the property will no longer be required for the purpose of any investigation or as evidence in any proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a person charged with a designated offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant acquired title to or a right of possession of the property from such a person under circumstances that give rise to a reasonable inference that the title or right was transferred from that person for the purpose of avoiding the forfeiture of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that a warrant should not have been issued under section 462.32 or 462.321 or a restraint order under subsection 462.33(3) should not have been made in respect of that property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is the lawful owner of or lawfully entitled to possession of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant appears innocent of any complicity in a designated offence or of any collusion in relation to such an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no other person appears to be the lawful owner of or lawfully entitled to possession of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.34(6) the conditions referred to in paragraph (4)(b) are satisfied` MEANS
    IF NOT `the property will no longer be required for the purpose of any investigation or as evidence in any proceeding`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the judge is satisfied that the property will no longer be required for the purpose of any investigation or as evidence in any proceeding"
    ELSE IF `the applicant is a person charged with a designated offence` OR `the applicant acquired title to or a right of possession of the property from such a person under circumstances that give rise to a reasonable inference that the title or right was transferred from that person for the purpose of avoiding the forfeiture of the property`
         THEN (IF `the judge is satisfied that a warrant should not have been issued under section 462.32 or 462.321 or a restraint order under subsection 462.33(3) should not have been made in respect of that property`
               THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a)
               ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that a warrant should not have been issued under section 462.32 or 462.321 or a restraint order under subsection 462.33(3) should not have been made in respect of that property"
         ELSE (IF `the applicant is the lawful owner of or lawfully entitled to possession of the property` AND `the applicant appears innocent of any complicity in a designated offence or of any collusion in relation to such an offence` AND `no other person appears to be the lawful owner of or lawfully entitled to possession of the property`
               THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b)
               ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that the applicant is the lawful owner of or lawfully entitled to possession of the property and appears innocent of any complicity in a designated offence or of any collusion in relation to such an offence"

-- src:8162 | (4) On an application made to a judge under paragraph (1)(a) in respect of any property and after hearing the applicant and the Attorney General and any other person to whom notice was given pursuant to paragraph (2)(b), the judge may order that the property or a part thereof be returned to the applicant or, in the case of a restraint order made under subsection 462.33(3), revoke the order, vary the order to exclude the property or any interest in the property or part thereof from the application of the order or make the order subject to such reasonable conditions as the judge thinks fit,
-- src:8163 | (a) if the applicant enters into a recognizance before the judge, with or without sureties, in such amount and with such conditions, if any, as the judge directs and, where the judge considers it appropriate, deposits with the judge such sum of money or other valuable security as the judge directs;
-- src:8164 | (b) if the conditions referred to in subsection (6) are satisfied; or
-- src:8165 | (c) for the purpose of
-- src:8166 | (i) meeting the reasonable living expenses of the person who was in possession of the property at the time the warrant was executed or the order was made or any person who, in the opinion of the judge, has a valid interest in the property and of the dependants of that person,
-- src:8167 | (ii) meeting the reasonable business and legal expenses of a person referred to in subparagraph (i), or
-- src:8168 | (iii) permitting the use of the property in relation to an undertaking or release order,
-- src:8169 | if the judge is satisfied that the applicant has no other assets or means available for the purposes set out in this paragraph and that no other person appears to be the lawful owner of or lawfully entitled to possession of the property.
@ref s 462.34(4) (src:8162-8169)
GIVEN `the application is made under paragraph (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge has heard the applicant and the Attorney General and any other person to whom notice was given pursuant to paragraph (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant enters into a recognizance before the judge, with or without sureties, in such amount and with such conditions, if any, as the judge directs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions referred to in subsection (6) are satisfied, by s 462.34(6) the conditions referred to in paragraph (4)(b) are satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is meeting the reasonable living expenses of the person who was in possession of the property or of any person who, in the opinion of the judge, has a valid interest in the property and of the dependants of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is meeting the reasonable business and legal expenses of such a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is permitting the use of the property in relation to an undertaking or release order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the applicant has no other assets or means available for the purposes set out in paragraph (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that no other person appears to be the lawful owner of or lawfully entitled to possession of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.34(4) the judge may order that the property be returned or the restraint order revoked or varied` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the application is made under paragraph (1)(a)` AND `the judge has heard the applicant and the Attorney General and any other person to whom notice was given pursuant to paragraph (2)(b)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On an application made to a judge under paragraph (1)(a) in respect of any property and after hearing the applicant and the Attorney General" (gates of the kinds "on an application" and "after ..." on a power: listed in the fork register, F35)
    ELSE IF `the applicant enters into a recognizance before the judge, with or without sureties, in such amount and with such conditions, if any, as the judge directs`   -- (a)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `the conditions referred to in subsection (6) are satisfied, by s 462.34(6) the conditions referred to in paragraph (4)(b) are satisfied` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE IF (`the purpose is meeting the reasonable living expenses of the person who was in possession of the property or of any person who, in the opinion of the judge, has a valid interest in the property and of the dependants of that person`   -- (c)(i)
                        OR `the purpose is meeting the reasonable business and legal expenses of such a person`   -- (c)(ii)
                        OR `the purpose is permitting the use of the property in relation to an undertaking or release order`)   -- (c)(iii)
                       AND `the judge is satisfied that the applicant has no other assets or means available for the purposes set out in paragraph (c)`
                       AND `the judge is satisfied that no other person appears to be the lawful owner of or lawfully entitled to possession of the property`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the judge may order that the property or a part thereof be returned to the applicant"

-- src:8171 | (5) For the purpose of determining the reasonableness of legal expenses referred to in subparagraph (4)(c)(ii), a judge shall hold an in camera hearing, without the presence of the Attorney General, and shall take into account the legal aid tariff of the province.
@ref s 462.34(5) (src:8171)
GIVEN `the purpose is determining the reasonableness of legal expenses referred to in subparagraph (4)(c)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hearing is held in camera` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hearing is held without the presence of the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge takes into account the legal aid tariff of the province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.34(5) the hearing is held as subsection (5) requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `the purpose is determining the reasonableness of legal expenses referred to in subparagraph (4)(c)(ii)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purpose of determining the reasonableness of legal expenses referred to in subparagraph (4)(c)(ii)"
    ELSE IF `the hearing is held in camera` AND `the hearing is held without the presence of the Attorney General` AND `the judge takes into account the legal aid tariff of the province`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a judge shall hold an in camera hearing, without the presence of the Attorney General, and shall take into account the legal aid tariff of the province"

DECLARE `s 462.34(5.1) representation` IS ONE OF
    `s 462.34(5.1)(a) at the hearing of the application, representations as to what would constitute the reasonableness of the expenses, other than legal expenses`
    `s 462.34(5.1)(b) before or after the hearing held in camera pursuant to subsection (5), representations as to what would constitute reasonable legal expenses referred to in subparagraph (4)(c)(ii)`
    `s 462.34(5.1) a representation that is none of those`

-- src:8173 | (5.1) For the purpose of determining the reasonableness of expenses referred to in paragraph (4)(c), the Attorney General may
-- src:8174 | (a) at the hearing of the application, make representations as to what would constitute the reasonableness of the expenses, other than legal expenses; and
-- src:8175 | (b) before or after the hearing of the application held in camera pursuant to subsection (5), make representations as to what would constitute reasonable legal expenses referred to in subparagraph (4)(c)(ii).
@ref s 462.34(5.1) (src:8173-8175)
GIVEN representation IS A `s 462.34(5.1) representation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.34(5.1) the Attorney General may make the representation` MEANS
    CONSIDER representation
    WHEN `s 462.34(5.1) a representation that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the Attorney General may"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:8177 | (5.2) The judge who made an order under paragraph (4)(c) may, and on the application of the Attorney General shall, tax the legal fees forming part of the legal expenses referred to in subparagraph (4)(c)(ii) and, in so doing, shall take into account
@ref s 462.34(5.2) (src:8177)
GIVEN `the judge made an order under paragraph (4)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.34(5.2) the judge may tax the legal fees` MEANS
    IF `the judge made an order under paragraph (4)(c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The judge who made an order under paragraph (4)(c) may"

@ref s 462.34(5.2) (src:8177)
GIVEN `the judge made an order under paragraph (4)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.34(5.2) the judge must tax the legal fees` MEANS
    IF `the judge made an order under paragraph (4)(c)` AND `the Attorney General has applied`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the application of the Attorney General shall"

DECLARE `s 462.34(5.2) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 462.34(5.2)(a) the value of property in respect of which an order of forfeiture may be made`
    `s 462.34(5.2)(b) the complexity of the proceedings giving rise to those legal expenses`
    `s 462.34(5.2)(c) the importance of the issues involved in those proceedings`
    `s 462.34(5.2)(d) the duration of any hearings held in respect of those proceedings`
    `s 462.34(5.2)(e) whether any stage of those proceedings was improper or vexatious`
    `s 462.34(5.2)(f) any representations made by the Attorney General`
    `s 462.34(5.2)(g) any other relevant matter`
    `s 462.34(5.2) a matter that is not relevant`

-- src:8177 | (5.2) The judge who made an order under paragraph (4)(c) may, and on the application of the Attorney General shall, tax the legal fees forming part of the legal expenses referred to in subparagraph (4)(c)(ii) and, in so doing, shall take into account
-- src:8178 | (a) the value of property in respect of which an order of forfeiture may be made;
-- src:8179 | (b) the complexity of the proceedings giving rise to those legal expenses;
-- src:8180 | (c) the importance of the issues involved in those proceedings;
