-- src:8195 | 462.341 Subsection 462.34(2), paragraph 462.34(4)(c) and subsections 462.34(5), (5.1) and (5.2) apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to a person who has an interest in money, bank-notes or virtual currency or other digital assets that are seized under this Act, the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or the Cannabis Act and in respect of which proceedings may be taken under subsection 462.37(1) or (2.01) or 462.38(2).
@ref s 462.341 (src:8195)
GIVEN `the person has an interest in money, bank-notes or virtual currency or other digital assets` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money, bank-notes or digital assets are seized under this Act, the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or the Cannabis Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proceedings may be taken in respect of them under subsection 462.37(1) or (2.01) or 462.38(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.341 subsection 462.34(2), paragraph 462.34(4)(c) and subsections 462.34(5), (5.1) and (5.2) apply to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person has an interest in money, bank-notes or virtual currency or other digital assets`
        AND `the money, bank-notes or digital assets are seized under this Act, the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act or the Cannabis Act`
        AND `proceedings may be taken in respect of them under subsection 462.37(1) or (2.01) or 462.38(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require, to a person who has an interest in money, bank-notes or virtual currency or other digital assets that are seized under this Act"

§§ `s 462.35 -- Expiration of special warrants and restraint orders`

-- "a period not exceeding six months from the seizure or the making of the order": the last day is the same day of the month six months later
-- (`Date` rolls an overflowing day forward, so six months from 31 August is 3 March; the Interpretation Act is not among the sources: see NOTES.md, fork register).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 462.35 the date six months after` MEANS Date (DATE_DAY d) (DATE_MONTH d PLUS 6) (DATE_YEAR d)

-- src:8197 | 462.35 (1) Subject to this section, if property has been seized under a warrant issued under section 462.32 or 462.321 or a restraint order has been made under section 462.33 in relation to property, the property may be detained or the order may continue in force, as the case may be, for a period not exceeding six months from the seizure or the making of the order, as the case may be.
@ref s 462.35(1) (src:8197)
GIVEN `the date of the seizure or of the making of the order` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.35(1) the property may be detained, or the order may continue in force, on the date asked about` MEANS
    IF `the date asked about` AT MOST `s 462.35 the date six months after` `the date of the seizure or of the making of the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period not exceeding six months from the seizure or the making of the order"

-- src:8199 | (2) The property may continue to be detained, or the order may continue in force, for a period that exceeds six months if proceedings are instituted in respect of which the thing detained may be forfeited.
@ref s 462.35(2) (src:8199)
GIVEN `proceedings are instituted in respect of which the thing detained may be forfeited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.35(2) the property may continue to be detained, or the order may continue in force, beyond six months` MEANS
    IF `proceedings are instituted in respect of which the thing detained may be forfeited`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if proceedings are instituted in respect of which the thing detained may be forfeited"

-- src:8201 | (3) The property may continue to be detained or the order may continue in force for a period or periods that exceed six months if the continuation is, on application made by the Attorney General, ordered by a judge, where the judge is satisfied that the property is required, after the expiration of the period or periods, for the purpose of section 462.37 or 462.38 or any other provision of this or any other Act of Parliament respecting forfeiture or for the purpose of any investigation or as evidence in any proceeding.
@ref s 462.35(3) (src:8201)
GIVEN `the continuation is, on application made by the Attorney General, ordered by a judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the property is required, after the expiration of the period or periods, for the purpose of section 462.37 or 462.38 or any other provision of this or any other Act of Parliament respecting forfeiture or for the purpose of any investigation or as evidence in any proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.35(3) the property may continue to be detained, or the order may continue in force, for a period or periods that exceed six months` MEANS
    IF `the continuation is, on application made by the Attorney General, ordered by a judge`
        AND `the judge is satisfied that the property is required, after the expiration of the period or periods, for the purpose of section 462.37 or 462.38 or any other provision of this or any other Act of Parliament respecting forfeiture or for the purpose of any investigation or as evidence in any proceeding`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the continuation is, on application made by the Attorney General, ordered by a judge, where the judge is satisfied"

-- Subsection (1) is "Subject to this section": the composition of (1), (2) and (3).
-- src:8197 | 462.35 (1) Subject to this section, if property has been seized under a warrant issued under section 462.32 or 462.321 or a restraint order has been made under section 462.33 in relation to property, the property may be detained or the order may continue in force, as the case may be, for a period not exceeding six months from the seizure or the making of the order, as the case may be.
-- src:8198 | Where proceedings instituted
-- src:8199 | (2) The property may continue to be detained, or the order may continue in force, for a period that exceeds six months if proceedings are instituted in respect of which the thing detained may be forfeited.
-- src:8200 | Where application made
-- src:8201 | (3) The property may continue to be detained or the order may continue in force for a period or periods that exceed six months if the continuation is, on application made by the Attorney General, ordered by a judge, where the judge is satisfied that the property is required, after the expiration of the period or periods, for the purpose of section 462.37 or 462.38 or any other provision of this or any other Act of Parliament respecting forfeiture or for the purpose of any investigation or as evidence in any proceeding.
@ref s 462.35(1) to (3) (src:8197-8201)
GIVEN `the answer of subsection (1), by s 462.35(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of subsection (2), by s 462.35(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of subsection (3), by s 462.35(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.35 the property may continue to be detained, or the order may continue in force` MEANS
    IF `the answer of subsection (1), by s 462.35(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer of subsection (2), by s 462.35(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer of subsection (3), by s 462.35(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the answer of subsection (1), by s 462.35(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period not exceeding six months from the seizure or the making of the order"
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (1) was not answered

§§ `s 462.36 -- Forwarding to clerk where accused to stand trial`

-- src:8203 | 462.36 If a judge issues a warrant under section 462.32 or 462.321 or makes a restraint order under section 462.33 in respect of any property, the clerk of the court shall, when an accused is ordered to stand trial for a designated offence, cause to be forwarded to the clerk of the court to which the accused has been ordered to stand trial a copy of the report filed under paragraph 462.32(4)(b) or 462.321(4)(c) or of the restraint order in respect of the property.
@ref s 462.36 (src:8203)
GIVEN `a judge issues a warrant under section 462.32 or 462.321 or makes a restraint order under section 462.33 in respect of any property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an accused is ordered to stand trial for a designated offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 462.36 the clerk of the court must forward a copy of the report or of the restraint order to the clerk of the court to which the accused has been ordered to stand trial` MEANS
    IF `a judge issues a warrant under section 462.32 or 462.321 or makes a restraint order under section 462.33 in respect of any property` AND `an accused is ordered to stand trial for a designated offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the clerk of the court shall, when an accused is ordered to stand trial for a designated offence, cause to be forwarded to the clerk of the court to which the accused has been ordered to stand trial a copy of the report"
